  "lineage": "Funeral song-dance of the Tujia of the middle Qingjiang valley in western Hubei (Changyang, Wufeng and Badong), performed through the night at the wake of an elder: a drummer beating a large drum beside the coffin leads the high-pitched songs, and the men who dance answer him; it is listed on China's national intangible-heritage register as a traditional dance. The acoustic membrane drum card stands in for the funeral drum.",
